 conducted in July, had Hurd ahead by a single point, and prediction markets give Romero roughly a 37 percent chance of winning. A favorable national environment for Democrats this year offsets much of the district's Republican lean, and coverage describes the race as increasingly competitive. A Libertarian and an independent are also on the ballot. Hurd remains the favorite, but the size of his edge is uncertain with so little fresh polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -3.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2864, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3508, "margin": -3.0}]}